     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello Shiny wizards!</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m comfortable with R, fairly friendly with Shiny, but weak in the JavaScript skillset.</div><div><br></div><div>My question: For elements that are built for you by Shiny, such as the element built by the radioButtons() function, is there a way to add popovers to or beside features of the element?</div><div><br></div><div>Let&#39;s use, for example, the really basic radioButtons demo provided in the <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/widget-gallery.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/widget-gallery.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399087402000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2DJ2MV4kZJk_UgIacZeoyy\">Shiny Widget Gallery</a>.</div><div><br></div><div><b>server.R</b></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;padding:9.5px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1em;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;border-style:none;border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:inherit;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">shinyServer</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,255)\">function</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">output</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span>\r\n\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># You can access the values of the widget (as a vector)</span>\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># with input$radio, e.g.</span>\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">output</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">value</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">renderPrint</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">{</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">input</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">radio</span> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">}</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre></div><div><b>ui.R</b></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;padding:9.5px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1em;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;border-style:none;border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:inherit;color:inherit;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">shinyUI</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fluidPage</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span>\r\n    \r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(76,136,107)\"># Copy the line below to make a set of radio buttons</span>\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">radioButtons</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;radio&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">label</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">h3</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Radio buttons&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>,\r\n    <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">choices</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">list</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Choice 1&quot;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,205)\">1</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Choice 2&quot;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,205)\">2</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;Choice 3&quot;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,205)\">3</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>, \r\n    <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">selected</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,205)\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>,\r\n  \r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">hr</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>,\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fluidRow</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">column</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,205)\">3</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">verbatimTextOutput</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(3,106,7)\">&quot;value&quot;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n  \r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span></code></pre></div><div>How would I go about modifying this code so that a user could click on each radio button choice (e.g., &quot;Choice 1&quot;) and get a text description of that choice (&quot;This is the first choice. Click it if you want to.&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>This is similar to the question posed <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/shiny-discuss/hover/shiny-discuss/6Jnmhpz5lJQ/_FyGSam50RwJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/shiny-discuss/hover/shiny-discuss/6Jnmhpz5lJQ/_FyGSam50RwJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399087403000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22qDbT4mck5iyOJLol9kZR\">here</a> about sliderInputs, which references the nifty <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/shinyBS/shinyBS.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/shinyBS/shinyBS.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399087403000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RKfj-mdIOamCnSOnLd5Iv\">shinyBS package</a>. However, the shinyBS solutions (bsPopover, popify, and addPopover) add popovers to an entire element. This is fine if you are generating a collection of separate elements (e.g., a set of sliders, each defined separately) but - as best I can tell - can&#39;t be used to specify popovers for features of an element.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance for any time and help you have to share!!</div><br><div>PS - This is my first post to the group - feel free to tell me if I&#39;m failing to follow any posting etiquette or best practice!</div></div>"
    ]
